<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Gemex, PepsiCo to buy Protexa unit.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Gemex, PepsiCo to buy Protexa unit.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican conglomerate Grupo Protexa SA said it agreed to sell its Agral bottling unit to Grupo Embotellador de Mexico SA (Gemex) and PepsiCo Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;We don't have details of the operation, but the buyers are Grupo Gemex and PepsiCo,&quot; Margarita Espino, a Protexa spokeswoman, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Gemex is PepsiCo's anchor bottler in Mexico. The U.S.-based company owns a 25 percent stake in Gemex.</p>
</text>
